      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, an average residential roof replacement takes one to three days for standard asphalt shingles. Smaller homes or simple roof layouts are often completed in a single day, while larger or more complex projects take up to three to five days.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "one to three days"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Time Factors"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Size & Pitch: Steep slopes, multiple valleys, or high square footage add time."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Materials:\nAsphalt shingles take 1\u20132 days, whereas metal roofing, tile, or wood shakes often require 3 to 5 days or more."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hidden Damage: Rotted plywood or structural decking discovered after the old material is torn off can extend the project."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Utah Weather:\nMountain weather shifts, high winds, or unexpected snow/rain can cause brief scheduling delays."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
